# Data directories (large generated/derived artifacts, not source) --
# academicos-data/ is ~9GB of parsed docs, indexes, scan sessions, sqlite
# DBs, etc. EXCEPT academicos-data/syllabus/*.json: real, hand-verified
# CBSE Class X curriculum data (syllabus/cbse_syllabus.py's own module
# docstring), tiny (~5KB total), and load-bearing -- every curriculum
# seed/extraction/scheduling path depends on it. Excluding it here broke
# CI and the deployed backend silently (subjects_seeded=0, /syllabus/*
# 404s) until caught by the deploy pipeline's own test gate.
academicos-data/*
!academicos-data/syllabus/
# The built CBSE CBE bank IS committed -- the app, the MCP server and CI all
# need it. Only the source PDFs are excluded, by the rule at the end of this
# file. Re-including the directory is required before that rule can bite.
!academicos-data/corpus/
# docs/research/ holds large raw research artifacts (a 6.4 MB PDF, a 234 KB
# text dump, attention/research notes) that should not be committed. The curated
# write-ups that live alongside them ARE project documentation -- they are
# referenced from docs/design-system.md and docs/PRODUCTS_AND_RELEASES.md -- so
# they are re-included explicitly. Note the `*`: ignoring the directory itself
# would make the negations below ineffective.
docs/research/*
!docs/research/ui-ux-principles.md
!docs/research/llm-layer.md
!docs/research/case-studies.md
!docs/research/interface-specification.md
!docs/research/production-ai-principles.md

# Large build artifacts / distributables (not source, don't belong in git)
*.zip
*.apk
desktop_dist/
frontend/build/
scratch_test/
pilot-corpus/

# Vendor/submodules
vendor/

# Temporary files created during testing
temp_*/
tmp_*/

# secrets — never commit
config/secrets.env
ncert-mcp-upstream/

# Logs
*.log

# Personal IDE workspace files — machine-specific, and *.code-workspace can
# reference folders outside the repo entirely (found live 2026-09-18: one
# committed here pointed at an unrelated personal directory on one dev's
# machine).
*.code-workspace

# One-off local test/eval artifacts that have been committed by accident
# before (2026-09-18: a hardcoded-path smoke-test database, a one-time eval
# run's CSV output) -- real, reusable eval tooling belongs under scripts/ or
# a dedicated results directory, not loose at the repo root.
/test_ingestion_state.db
/eval_rag_results.csv

# The CBSE CBE item-bank source PDFs. Deliberately NOT committed: they are
# third-party government documents whose redistribution position is unresolved
# (docs/question-bank-api.md section 2), and committing them into the repository
# would be redistribution to everyone with repo access -- the exact act the
# unresolved question is about.
#
# The download is reproducible instead: scripts/ingest_cbse_item_banks.py
# fetches all 15 from the URL CBSE publishes, and the committed `_manifest.json`
# records what was fetched, when, and with what rights status. The derived
# `questions.json` IS committed, because the app and CI need it and it holds
# only the extracted questions and marking schemes.
academicos-data/corpus/cbse-cbe/*.pdf
academicos-data/corpus/cbse-cbe/_unanswerable.json

# SQP+MS source PDFs: same position, same reasoning as the CBE PDFs above.
# scripts/ingest_sqp_ms.py re-fetches them from the published URL and the
# committed _manifest.json records what was fetched and with what rights status.
academicos-data/corpus/cbse-sqp/*/*.pdf


# Firebase CLI deploy cache, written by `firebase deploy` (docs/deploy-by-hand.md).
.firebase/
